  "delta": {
    "direct_http_default": "CHANGED: isolated default and v2-only now use modern discover and catalog listen, without MCP_PROTOCOL_NEGOTIATION=auto. Official 2.1.274 notes document the default change for telemetry-disabled and third-party provider installs.",
    "default_change_release": "https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/releases/tag/v2.1.274",
    "tasks": "UNCHANGED: no declared legacy tasks or tasks extension in any case; gF() remains literally false; only the legacy task methods and status notification are bundled.",
    "listen": "Catalog notification refetch and dropped-stream reopen/reconciliation remain functional.",
    "opt_out": "MCP_SDK_GENERATION=v1 or MCP_PROTOCOL_NEGOTIATION=legacy each restores initialize at 2025-11-25.",
    "unmatched_ack": "Initial acknowledgement timeout remains about 25 s. The client now attempts a replacement listen through its reopen machinery after continuing with catalog listing; this probe does not establish successful acknowledgement on the replacement."
  },
  "methodology": {
    "static": "Exact-byte counts and bounded inspection of readable embedded JavaScript. Literal vocabulary presence is not proof of reachable behavior. Counts increased with bundle layout changes and are not feature counts.",
    "live": "Unmodified installed binary, --bare -p, --tools '' (empty built-in tool set), --setting-sources '', --strict-mcp-config, explicit loopback-only MCP fixture, --debug-file. Each case used a fresh temporary cwd and CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR under env -i with HOME preserved; CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, --bare, empty setting sources and strict MCP config provide fixture isolation. ANTHROPIC_API_KEY was a dummy value and ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL pointed to a local deterministic Messages stub holding its first response for 8 s so list-change delivery was observable. No real model inference or shared-service mutation. Fixtures: fixtures/claude-mcp-fixture.py, fixtures/claude-messages-stub.py, fixtures/claude-audit-matrix.sh.",
    "fixture": "Discover advertised 2026-07-28 and 2025-11-25, all three catalog listChanged capabilities, resources.subscribe and the io.modelcontextprotocol/tasks extension. Listen answered as chunked SSE with the acknowledgement first, its subscription id equal to the listen request id, then tools/resources/prompts list_changed after waiting up to 10 s for the first tools/list and another 1 s. Healthy cases list before emission; in the unmatched-ack case the bounded wait expires, so the first notifications precede catalog startup at about 25 s. The legacy fixture rejected discover with -32601 and answered initialize at the requested version with Mcp-Session-Id and legacy tasks advertised, holding the GET stream. The drop fixture closed the first listen stream right after the notifications with no terminal JSON-RPC result. The unmatched-ack case substitutes a server-minted subscription id. Four added cases cover default fallback, each explicit legacy opt-out, and mismatched acknowledgement.",
    "limits": [
      "Account-specific remote rollout flags were not inspected; isolated defaults are not a universal rollout verdict.",
      "Prompt/resource catalogs were empty; only tool refetches were observed after list_changed notifications.",
      "No task result was returned to a client that did not declare support. Task execution and task notifications were not tested.",
      "No per-URI resource subscription, MRTR elicitation interaction, or prolonged reconnect/parking behavior was live-tested.",
      "The claude.ai connector projection headers were decoded statically only; no claude.ai connector was contacted.",
      "No tools/call was induced by the deterministic text-only model stub; this matrix verifies negotiation, catalogs and listen."
    ],
    "raw_evidence_directory": "/tmp/claude-2.1.280-mcp-audit-20260922-preserved-home",
    "capture_validation": "All nine cases passed a fresh full matrix with HOME preserved and EXPECT_TASKS=absent; the saved captures also passed AUDIT_VERIFY_ONLY=1 replay. The verifier requires successful CLI exit/result, nonempty MCP traffic, model requests, protocol metadata, catalogs, explicit-selector lifecycles, notification refetches, stream reopen/reconciliation and unmatched-ack cancellation. Default lifecycle and task capabilities are observed unless explicitly pinned. Negative replays with an empty capture, missing model request, missing tool refetch or missing cancellation each exited 1; a live matrix using /usr/bin/false also exited 1."
  },
